senses.gloss:
1. उप-√ 1. दा P. -ददाति, to give in addition, add;
to give, grant, offer, RV. vi, 28, 2; AV. iv, 21, 2; xix, 34, 8; R.;
to take upon one's self:
Pass. (irr. p. -दद्य॑मान) to be offered or granted (as protection), RV. vi, 49, 13.

उपा-√ 1. दा Ā. -दत्ते, (once P. pf. 3. pl. -ददुस्, BhP. i, 8, 12) to receive, accept, gain, acquire, appropriate to one's self, take away, carry off, steal, MBh.; BhP.; Mālav. &c. ;
to take with;
to take in addition, include, comprise;
to take as help, use, employ, apply, BhP.; Pat. (cf. उपा-दाय);
to seize, lay hold of, gather, take up, draw up, MBh.; Ragh.; Kum. &c.;
to assume (a form or meaning), BhP.; MārkP.; Pat. &c.;
to cling to;
to feel, perceive, experience, MBh. vii; Śiś. vi, 23; Ṛtus. &c.;
to consider, regard, MBh. xii;
to mention, enumerate;
to set about, undertake, begin, Hariv.; Kum. &c.:
Caus. P. -दापयति, to cause to use or employ Comm. on KātyŚr.:
Desid. P. -दित्सति, to strive to acquire, BhP. v, 14, 7.

1. उप-√ दिश् P. Ā. -दिशति, -ते, to point out to, ŚBr. x, 6, 1, 11;
to indicate, specify, explain, inform, instruct, teach, ŚBr.; ĀśvŚr. & ĀśvGṛ.; MBh.; Mṛcch.; Ragh. &c.;
to advise, admonish, BhP.; Hit.;
to mention, exhibit, speak of BhP.; Mn.; Mṛcch.; VPrāt. &c.;
to settle, prescribe, command, dictate, govern, MBh.; Mn.; Kum.; Pañcat. &c.;
to name, call, MBh.; BhP.; Mn. &c. :
Pass. -दिश्यते, to be taught, &c.

1. उप-√ दृश् P. (aor. Subj. 2. du. -दर्शथस्, RV.) to descry, perceive, RV. viii, 26, 4;
to look at or regard (with indifference), MBh. :
Pass. -दृश्यते (aor. -अदर्शि; 3. pl. -अदृश्रन्, RV.)
to be perceived, be or become visible, appear, RV. i, 124, 4; vii, 67, 2; TāṇḍyaBr.; BhP. :
Caus. -दर्शयति, to cause to see, show, exhibit, MBh.; Ragh.; Kathās.; Prab. &c.;
to cause to appear, present a false show, deceive, illude, Kathās. xix, 75; Rājat.;
to explain, illustrate, Yājñ. ii, 8.

उप-√ द्रु P. -द्रवति (aor. -अ॑दुद्रोत्, RV.) to run near or towards;
to run at, rush at, oppress, assault, attack, RV. ii, 30, 3; iv, 16, 1; AV. vii, 73, 6; xviii, 2, 23; TS.; ChUp.;
to sing the Upa-drava or fourth of the five parts of a Sāman stanza, AitĀr. ii, 3, 4, 3.
